<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0;netstandard2.1</TargetFrameworks>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <WarnOn>3390</WarnOn>
    <OtherFlags>$(OtherFlags) --reflectionfree</OtherFlags>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU1900</NoWarn>
    <PackageId>Flap</PackageId>
    <Version>0.0.2-rc1</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Initial release of Flap, a clap-style fluent CLI parser for F#: `Arg` and `Command` builders, `Matches` with typed getters, help/version output, did-you-mean suggestions and shell completions (Bash, Zsh, Fish, PowerShell, Nushell).
Native AOT (reflection-free) and Fable compatibility, with samples.
`Matches.getWith`, `getInt`, `getBool` and `getFloat`: required typed getters returning `Result&lt;'T, string&gt;`.
`Arg.allowHyphenValues`: options and positionals may take values starting with `-`.
`Arg.trailingVarArg`: the last multi-value positional takes every remaining token verbatim (for exec-style wrappers like `tool run cmd --flag`). `Command.check` rejects it on any other arg.
Help customization: `Command.longAbout`, `Command.beforeHelp`, `Command.afterHelp` and `Arg.helpHeading`.
Value-aware shell completions: possible values complete for options and positionals, and the new `Arg.valueHint` (`ValueHint`: `AnyPath`, `FilePath`, `DirPath`, `Other`) completes file system paths.
Dynamic completion building blocks: `Arg.completer` / `Arg.completerValues` attach a runtime completer to an arg, and the pure `Complete.candidates`, `Complete.envVarName` and `Complete.render` compute and format candidates (the per-app `&lt;NAME&gt;_COMPLETE` protocol). `Command.parse`/`parseWith` answer a completion request when `&lt;NAME&gt;_COMPLETE=&lt;shell&gt;` is set, printing candidates and exiting 0; apps that call `Command.tryParse` directly use the pure `Complete.respond`. Generated scripts for every shell (Bash, Zsh, Fish, PowerShell, Nushell) call back into the program only for args that have a completer; apps without one get unchanged static scripts. The `Shell` type now lives in `Types.fs` (same namespace, no API change).
`Command.subcommandNegatesRequired`: when a subcommand is given, the parent's required args and required groups are not enforced (like clap's `subcommand_negates_reqs`), so `tool &lt;input&gt;` can coexist with `tool completions &lt;shell&gt;`.
Nushell completions (`Completions.generate Nushell`), generated as `extern` definitions with `@` completers.
`mise.toml` pinning nushell, powershell and fish for smoke-testing the generated completion scripts.
Release automation: `./publish.sh` bumps the version, updates the changelog and tags; the tag-triggered `publish-nuget.yml` workflow publishes the `Flap` package to NuGet through Trusted Publishing. The package now carries its metadata and README.
**Breaking:** `Matches.tryInt`, `tryBool` and `tryFloat` now return `Result&lt;'T option, string&gt;` instead of silently turning an invalid value into `None`. Match on the `Result`, or use the new `getInt`/`getBool`/`getFloat`.
Completions now include global args inherited by subcommands, and PowerShell completion handles subcommand aliases.
The missing-subcommand error no longer wraps its message in stray quotes.
Environment variable values for flag args (`SetTrue`/`SetFalse`) are parsed as booleans, so `MYAPP_DEBUG=1` now reads as true.
An invalid environment variable value is now reported as an `InvalidValue` error naming the variable, instead of being silently dropped.
`Arg.numArgs` minimum is now enforced for positional arguments (`TooFewValues`).
Fish completions no longer leak the continuation lines of multi-line help text as bogus candidates; help is collapsed to a single line.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Devon Burriss</Authors>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>fsharp;cli;command-line;parser;clap;aot;fable</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dburriss/flap</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dburriss/flap</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <Description>A clap-inspired, pipe-friendly command line parser for F#. Native AOT and Fable compatible.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Types.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Arg.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Matches.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Help.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Parser.fs" />
    <Compile Include="CompletionModel.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Complete.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Completions.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Command.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>